# FEAT specs are PUBLIC as of 2026-07-29 (they were excluded until then).
# The design rationale in them is the most useful thing this repo has for a
# contributor trying to understand why the code looks the way it does, and 23
# of them were in public git history anyway — the exclusion was protecting
# very little.
#
# What that makes load-bearing, because a spec is now a published document:
#   - no private infrastructure (hosts, internal repo/script names, cron
#     detail), no developer home paths, no third-party contact data;
#   - third-party interoperability findings state the CONCLUSION, not a
#     step-by-step account of someone else's software;
#   - audit output stays out entirely — see the triage rule below.
# The 0.1.2–0.2.2 specs were redacted against exactly this list on 2026-07-29
# before the rule flipped.

# Internal triage workflow (RepoLens findings, verdicts, per-release audits)
#
# HARD RULE: RepoLens findings and any audit-tool output NEVER land in this
# repo. Always output to an absolute path under ~/cruxcoach-internal-archive/
# or similar — see CLAUDE.md "RepoLens and other audit tools" for the policy.
# The patterns below are a defence-in-depth backstop, not the primary control.
docs/specs/*/triage/
tools/triage/
scripts/repolens-*.sh

# RepoLens output shapes (file-name-based backstop across the whole tree)
findings.jsonl
verdicts.jsonl
**/findings.jsonl
**/verdicts.jsonl
repolens-out/
**/repolens-out/
**/repolens-run-*/
**/.repolens/

